notes 

Separating code into dedicated folders (models, routes, controllers) follows the principle of separation of concerns, keeping large codebases clean, debuggable, and scalable.

The 'models' folder holds schema definitions and database models (e.g., NoteSchema, UserSchema), representing the data layer of the MVC pattern.

Routes define the available API endpoints (URLs and HTTP methods like GET, POST) and connect each request to its corresponding controller function.


